    println!();
    println!("SELECTION SYNTAX AND USAGE");
    println!();
    println!("Selections are used to select atoms/molecules/residues for analysis. In");
    println!("contrast to traditional index files, selections can be dynamic, i.e., select");
    println!("different atoms for different trajectory frames. The GROMACS manual contains a");
    println!("short introductory section to selections in the Analysis chapter, including");
    println!("suggestions on how to get familiar with selections if you are new to the");
    println!("concept. The subtopics listed below provide more details on the technical and");
    println!("syntactic aspects of selections.");
    println!();
    println!("Each analysis tool requires a different number of selections and the");
    println!("selections are interpreted differently. The general idea is still the same:");
    println!("each selection evaluates to a set of positions, where a position can be an");
    println!("atom position or center-of-mass or center-of-geometry of a set of atoms. The");
    println!("tool then uses these positions for its analysis to allow very flexible");
    println!("processing. Some analysis tools may have limitations on the types of");
    println!("selections allowed.");
    println!();
    println!("Available subtopics:");
